---
import CartButton from '../components/CartButton.astro';
import DownloadButton from '../components/DownloadButton.astro';
import SubscribeForm from '../components/SubscribeForm.astro';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

// A stand-in for your data: a CMS, a database, read when the page is built.
const products = [
    { id: 1, name: 'Headphones', price: '$129', inCart: true },
    { id: 2, name: 'Keyboard', price: '$89', inCart: false },
];
---

<Layout title="Scripts">
    <h1>Icons that follow your scripts</h1>
    <p class="lead">
        Astro puts the state in the HTML, as an attribute, and a few lines of{' '}
        <code>&lt;script&gt;</code> change it; <code>trigger="follow"</code> keeps the icon in step.
        No framework, no event wiring for the icon itself.
    </p>

    <h2>A toggle, from the page's data</h2>
    <p class="note">
        Each button carries <code>aria-pressed</code>, set from the page's data when it is built,
        and the headphones are in the cart from the start: their icon starts on the second look,
        without playing. A click flips the attribute, and the icon morphs.
    </p>
    <ul class="products">
        {products.map((product) => (
            <li class="product">
                <span>
                    {product.name} <span class="price">{product.price}</span>
                </span>
                <CartButton inCart={product.inCart} />
            </li>
        ))}
    </ul>

    <h2>A process, in stages</h2>
    <p class="note">
        <code>follow(data-state, busy=loop-cycle, done=morph-check)</code> gives each value its
        animation: a loop while busy, a check when done, and back.
    </p>
    <div class="actions">
        <DownloadButton />
    </div>

    <h2>Played from code, after an action</h2>
    <p class="note">
        <code>querySelector('lord-icon')</code> gives the element, with <code>play()</code>. The
        form calls an Astro action on the server, and the icon plays when the server has answered.
    </p>
    <SubscribeForm />

    <p class="next">
        <a href="/server-rendering" class="link">
            Next: server rendering →
        </a>
    </p>
</Layout>

<style>
    .products {
        max-width: 480px;
        margin-top: 16px;
        list-style: none;
    }

    .product {
        display: flex;
        gap: 16px;
        align-items: center;
        justify-content: space-between;
        padding: 12px 0;
        border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    }

    .price {
        margin-left: 6px;
        color: var(--muted);
    }

    .next {
        margin-top: 48px;
    }
</style>
